# `steps[i & 1](i)` in a loop: two closures are held of the element, and that is no proof: each is tested for and its body is copied in behind its test; what fails both tests leaves
# for the loop that calls a value, so that the loop in front calls nothing. Outside a loop, and off a list of nine, the call stays one call of a value.
